# Snapshot (idle H200, GPU 0); reproduce with `python -m bench.eval --set all`. 74 of the full
# 105-config suite shown here; all 105 numerically correct, full-suite geomean ~1.17x (95/105 >=0.95x).
# The formerly-slow corners, now closed:
#   * fp8 head_dim 256 (dense + decode): a NATIVE fp8 hd256 wgmma path -- RS-PV (P in registers) at
#     CN=128/STAGES=2 + a COALESCED fp8 K/V gather (TPR8=HD/16 lanes/key + __shfl page resolve) --
#     replaced the bf16-convert fallback -> 0.196/0.342 -> 0.923/1.015x (dense prefill / kv decode).
#   * the SOL-ExecBench real GQA shapes (h32, page_size 1): a COALESCED cooperative K/V gather at FA3's
#     kGmemThreadsPerRow=8 granularity (128-byte single-cache-line bursts) + barrier-free __shfl page
#     resolve + LPT causal tile order + dropping the redundant per-tile fence.proxy.async lifted the family
#     to ~0.86-0.92. The BIG closer: FA3 PagedKVManager's offset-broadcast -- the int64 K/V row offset
#     (ent*stride) is computed ONCE by each row's resolving lane and shfl-broadcast (64-bit) to the 8
#     cooperating lanes, instead of all 8 recomputing it (8x redundant int64 muls that were thinning the
#     cp.async issue stream). This closed paged decode (llama8b_dec 0.91->0.96, qwen3moe_dec_s32k 0.95->0.99)
#     and qwen prefill (0.91->0.95), and lifted llama8b_pf +5pp (0.86/0.87 -> 0.91/0.93). Also matched FA3's
#     PV wgmma shape: one m64n128k16 (transB) instead of 2x m64n64.
#   * dense bf16 hd256 (0.88->0.95): ported FA3's SEPARATE K/V async-pipeline structure into the per-tile
#     mainloop (SPLITKV). FA3 (mainloop_fwd_sm90) runs distinct pipeline_k/pipeline_v and releases K right
#     after the QK gemm (warpgroup_wait<1>), a full PV-gemm BEFORE V -- so its producer refills K deep enough
#     to hide the 80KB load at kStages=2, which lets the wide CN=80 tile fit (single combined-ring STAGES=2
#     starved: long_scoreboard 2.28). We now use full_k/full_v/empty_k/empty_v barriers + staggered release
#     (empty_k at wgmma_wait1, empty_v at wgmma_wait0) at CN=80/STAGES=2. NCU: long_scoreboard 2.28->1.17,
#     barrier 3.62->0.72, compute 40->50% -> 0.75x->~0.95x. NCU had earlier disproved the "register/occupancy"
#     theory: FA3 and we BOTH run 1 CTA/SM at 18.75% (168 regs + 213KB smem); the gap was purely the 2-stage
#     load-hiding that the separate K pipeline unlocks. Gated to HD==256 && CM==128 && USE_TMA (dense prefill).
#   Remaining sub-0.95: llama8b_pf (0.92/0.95; NCU: FA3's persistent scheduler amortizes the pipeline-fill
#     prologue across a continuous ring, our per-tile grid pays it ~8 waves -- paged-persist replication
#     regressed on barrier overhead 1.46 vs 0.44). The SPLITKV separate-pipeline structure is the same lever
#     that would close it, ported to the paged/persistent path (future work).
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
